    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9760" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concătēnātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		concateno, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a connecting, joining</i> (late Lat.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var.
				12, 19</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<i>A concatenation, sequence</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">temporum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 19</span></i>
			: causarum, Aug. Civ. Dei, 3, 30.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> Mentis (i. e. constrictio), <i>fettering, binding</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Tard. 3, 2, 15</span></i>.</div>
